      {
        "n": "NTS Guide to: ESP-Disk - The Early Years",
        "s": "2026-08-23T15:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-08-23T18:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "Existing at the intersection of free jazz, acid folk, spoken word and avant garage rock, ESP-Disk opened for business in New York City at the zenith of 60's counter culture. \nThe label's first release was an Esperanto album, giving it the name ESP-Disk, and then released a number of free jazz albums that we would now consider classics. It soon came to champion other similarly less-commercial genres, always giving free reign to the artists. \nThis Guide To includes music from Sun Ra, Albert Ayler, William Burroughs, The Fugs and more.",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/the-nts-guide-to/episodes/the-nts-guide-to-esp-disk---the-early-years-6th-february-2024"
      },
